  "verbalization": "Miconioside A appears to exert its biological effects through a series of molecular interactions that ultimately target the CD276 antigen. The evidence suggests that Miconioside A acts as a target for multiple compounds, including 7-O-Methylmangiferin and Agallochin F, which in turn inhibit the CD276 antigen. This indicates a potential pathway where Miconioside A may modulate the activity of these compounds, which themselves are known to interact with CD276. The cumulative evidence from the three paths supports a mechanism where Miconioside A indirectly influences CD276 through the action of other molecules, suggesting a possible role in regulating CD276 expression or function. The integration of these pathways highlights the complexity of the relationship, with Miconioside A potentially serving as a modulator in this network. The observed scores suggest a consistent and plausible link, though further validation would be needed to confirm the direct interaction between Miconioside A and CD276.",
